meta {
  name: password reset request
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/password-reset/request
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "identifier": "{{adminEmail}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 202
}

docs {
  Requires no authentication — see the folder-level docs on why. Answers
  202 whether or not the identifier matches an account; errors/
  password-reset-request-unknown-identifier.bru is the same request for an
  address that does not exist, asserting the identical response.

  This collection has no mailbox to read, so — like invitations/
  accept-invitation.bru's own limitation, but without that endpoint's
  workaround — there is no request here that redeems the resulting token:
  the response never contains it, on purpose (see the endpoint's own
  description), so nothing in an HTTP-only test suite can recover it.
  errors/password-reset-confirm-invalid-token.bru covers what the confirm
  endpoint does with a token it does not have.
}
